{# ── 5. The Authorship & Local-First Ethos ── #}
<section class="not-prose mb-8 animate-enter stagger-5" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
    <h2 id="philosophy-heading" class="editorial-title">Transparency & Authorship Policy</h2>
    <span class="font-mono text-[0.78rem] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Guiding Rules</span>
  </div>
  <div class="surface rounded-sm p-4 md:p-6 border border-surface-border editorial-support leading-relaxed">
    <p class="mb-3">
      This site is an authored personal workbench, not an automated content mill. I use AI aggressively as a research amplifier, coding co-pilot, and terminal partner, but under strict boundaries:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 font-serif text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>
        <strong>Explicit Frontmatter Badges:</strong> Every note, post, and guide carries an immutable <code>authored_by</code> property (<code>human</code>, <code>ai-assisted</code>, or <code>ai-generated</code>) displayed in the entry metadata.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reader-Controlled AI Filter:</strong> The top navigation bar includes an interactive filter widget (<a href="/static/js/ai-filter.js" class="accent-link"><code>ai-filter.js</code></a>) allowing you to toggle between All content, Hide AI-generated, and Human-written only.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Zero Em Dashes & High Contraction Fingerprint:</strong> All prose is calibrated against my measured human writing fingerprint to eradicate robotic cadence, synthetic corporate framing, and chatbot residue.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local-First & Compression:</strong> Whenever possible, private code and experimental workflows stay on consumer silicon. Constraints are the only reason computing advances.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
